[E0431] Error: `items` is `Vec<Plain>`, which cannot be compared
    ╭─[ err/137_comparison/main.wip:14:17 ]
    │
 13 │ @derive(Eq)
    │         ─┬
    │          ╰── `@derive(Eq)` writes the comparison field by field
 14 │ struct Holder { items: Vec<Plain> }
    │                 ────────┬────────
    │                         ╰────────── not a comparable field
    │
    │ Help 1: `Vec<Plain>` implements `Eq` where `Plain` does, and `Plain` does not
    │
    │ Help 2: write `@derive(Eq)` on `Plain` too, or an `extend` block that implements `Eq` for it
    │
    │ Note: a field is comparable when it is a number, a `bool`, a `str`, a `cstring`, a `ptr<T>`, an array of those, or a type that implements `Eq`
────╯
